refentry.refsect1:
&reftitle.parameters;
closure
The function to blacklist, represented as a first class callable. It is also possible to pass an anonymous function, in which case the anonymous function itself is blacklisted.

&reftitle.errors;
Throws a TypeError if closure is not a Closure.
The call is a silent no-op when PHP is built without JIT support, when closure does not wrap user code, or when the function has not been trace-compiled yet. Neither the return value nor any diagnostic distinguishes these cases.

  &reftitle.examples;


    opcache_jit_blacklist
    basic example



<?php
function foo() {
	$x = 1;
	$x += 0;
	++$x;
	var_dump($x);
}
opcache_jit_blacklist(foo(...));
foo();
?>


   &example.outputs;


int(2)
